{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789856030,"nonce":"aXiwQ152CyOv3A7hdW3WwL0FiT0=","title":"Lua: builtins resolve statically, whatever the environment holds","message":"print, pcall, rawget and every other base builtin are bound at compile time (builtin_named), so after _ENV = {} or in a chunk loaded with an env table lacking them they still work, where the reference finds nil. A program that shadows a builtin with a global assignment is handled (global_writes), one that replaces the environment is not. Would need dynamic_globals mode to resolve builtins through the environment table as well, at the cost of a table lookup per call in that mode.","files":null}]}